    <bpmn:process id="W_W4928" name="W4928. Separation / End-of-Employment Uniform Return &amp; Recovery" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Employee separation/resignation/termination (VS-19.5); contingent engagement-end (VS-98)
Frequency: Per separation (~1,000–1,340 exits/yr)
Volume: ~1,000–1,340 exits/yr × uniform/PPE return
Owner: HR Shared Services (VS-103) / Store Manager / Uniform Program Manager
Participants: HR (VS-19.5), Store Ops (VS-07), Asset Mgmt (VS-35), Finance (W4916), Contingent Lead (VS-98)
Source: workflow W4928 — Separation / End-of-Employment Uniform Return &amp; Recovery</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4928_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4928_Lane1" name="HRSS">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4928_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4928_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4928_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4928_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4928_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4928_Start3" name="Employee separation/resignation/termination (VS-19.5); contingent engagement-end (VS-98)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4928_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4928_Task4" name="Generate the uniform/PPE return list at separation (links VS-19.5 clearance)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Generate the uniform/PPE return list at separation (links VS-19.5 clearance): from the asset record (VS-35), list all BuildRight-issued uniform/PPE outstanding for the exiting employee; integrate into the clearance process (no final-pay release until cleared or charged per W4916)
Responsible (R): HRSS / Asset Mgmt / Program Manager
Accountable (A): Program Manager
Duration: Per separation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4928_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4928_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4928_Task5" name="Collect, inspect &amp; disposition: collect returned items, inspect for…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Collect, inspect &amp; disposition: collect returned items, inspect for damage/reusability, recondition/launder for reuse (W4924), retire destroyed/expired PPE (W4925), update the asset register (VS-35), and charge non-returned/damaged items per policy (W4916) with due process (VS-84)
Responsible (R): HRSS / Facilities / Asset Mgmt / Finance
Accountable (A): Program Manager
Duration: Per separation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4928_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4928_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4928_Task6" name="Manage exceptions &amp; contingent/vendor return: handle non-return (charge/debt…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Manage exceptions &amp; contingent/vendor return: handle non-return (charge/debt recovery, LP if theft VS-23), contingent/vendor-personnel asset return (W4923), and ensure brand-security (returned branded items not misused by ex-employees — branding/trademark VS-100.2)
Responsible (R): HRSS / LP / Legal / Program Manager
Accountable (A): Program Manager
Duration: Per separation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4928_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4928_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4928_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4928_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4928_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-132 (ensure PPE issuance &amp; DOLE compliance.) | - CTL-738: return-list from asset record; final-pay clearance per policy + due process (VS-84); inspected/dispositioned; brand-security on non-return
Owner: HR Shared Services (VS-103) / Store Manager / Uniform Program Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
